WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
Where you keep your emergency fund matters almost as much as how much you save.

00:10.000 --> 00:24.000
Keep it separate from your checking account, so it isn't mixed in with money for daily spending.

00:24.000 --> 00:42.000
A high-yield savings account is a good fit. It pays much more than a regular savings account, so your cushion grows a little while it waits.

00:42.000 --> 01:00.000
Make sure the account is insured: the FDIC insures banks, and the NCUA insures credit unions. Insurance protects your money, up to the legal limit, even if the institution runs into trouble.

01:00.000 --> 01:18.000
Keep it in savings, not in investments. Investments can drop in value right when you need cash.

01:18.000 --> 01:32.000
Look for low or no fees, and no minimum balance that's hard to meet.

01:32.000 --> 01:45.000
Once it's set up, move money in regularly. Even small amounts add up.
